that prepares you for the world

00:10:16.764 --> 00:10:19.874
You know? My mother had
a really bad childhood.

00:10:19.874 --> 00:10:22.144
And my father had a bad
childhood. And I had a bad

00:10:22.144 --> 00:10:24.951
childhood, but I love my childhood.

00:10:24.951 --> 00:10:27.263
Even though it was bad, I
love it. I feel like it's

00:10:27.263 --> 00:10:29.394
taught me so much.

00:10:29.394 --> 00:10:33.031
And I feel like nothing can
phase me. Nothing in this world

00:10:33.031 --> 00:10:36.900
nothing can surprise me.
It might set me back,

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.050
but only momentarily. Only to spring back.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:42.677
And I think it's helped me to learn.

00:10:42.677 --> 00:10:44.018
It really did help me to learn.

00:10:44.018 --> 00:10:45.925
And since my mother had a bad childhood,

00:10:45.925 --> 00:10:48.337
she knows the importance of being honest.

00:10:48.337 --> 00:10:52.269
And the importance of facing
each situation as it comes.

00:10:52.269 --> 00:10:54.033
And not dealing in a fairy tale land.

00:10:54.033 --> 00:10:56.172
Being realistic about the problem, and

00:10:56.172 --> 00:10:58.371
analyzing it and solving
it. Seeing what you can

00:10:58.371 --> 00:10:59.559
do to solve it.

00:10:59.559 --> 00:11:02.230
So, if you have a happy
childhood, you tend to

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:04.444
want your child to have a happy childhood.

00:11:04.444 --> 00:11:07.720
So, you tend to want to
keep the bad things out,

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.027
and I don't think that's good because then

00:11:09.027 --> 00:11:10.799
you're not prepared for the world.

00:11:10.799 --> 00:11:13.318
- [Interviewer] So basically,
you have to be realistic

00:11:13.318 --> 00:11:14.568
with your kids?

00:11:16.174 --> 00:11:18.854
- You should tell 'em. But
don't get the wrong idea,

00:11:18.854 --> 00:11:20.194
I feel like I'm being gloomy.

00:11:20.194 --> 00:11:23.124
I don't need to be just like,
everything's bad out there,

00:11:23.124 --> 00:11:25.846
but when the good things come
and they are going to come

00:11:25.846 --> 00:11:27.517
and everybody knows that.
Good things are going to come

00:11:27.517 --> 00:11:28.867
And you're going to see em
for yourself, you're going to

00:11:28.867 --> 00:11:31.675
see you did good. But it's
harder to see the bad things.

00:11:31.675 --> 00:11:33.699
And everybodyss going
to shield the bad things

00:11:33.699 --> 00:11:36.967
and that's where it gets
complicated and it gets rotten.

00:11:36.967 --> 00:11:38.718
That's where everybody gets surprised and

00:11:38.718 --> 00:11:40.883
Oh my god, I'm committin'
suicide, that's too much

00:11:40.883 --> 00:11:43.563
overwhelming. If you know
about it, it won't be so

00:11:43.563 --> 00:11:46.773
overwhelming. You know? So
that's what I think about that.

00:11:46.773 --> 00:11:51.083
All BS aside, it all comes
down to we got to survive.

00:11:51.083 --> 00:11:54.124
I mean, even warriors put
their spears down on Sundays.

00:11:54.124 --> 00:11:56.374
We got to survive here in this country.

00:11:56.374 --> 00:11:59.173
'Cause I'm not going back to
Africa. We got to survive here.

00:11:59.173 --> 00:12:02.567
For us to survive here,
white folks, black folks,

00:12:02.567 --> 00:12:05.624
Korean folks, Mexican folks,
Puerto Ricans, we got to

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:08.261
understand each other. We
got to take a bigger chance.

00:12:08.261 --> 00:12:10.259
And when I say Americans,
people think I'm talking

00:12:10.259 --> 00:12:13.236
about uncle Sam. I mean like
actually Uncle Sam, with the

00:12:13.236 --> 00:12:14.900
gray hair and the flag.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.733
I mean, you, you, you.
The guy, you know, you.

00:12:20.209 --> 00:12:24.273
The mechanic, wherever, you, I
mean you need to do somethin'

00:12:24.273 --> 00:12:25.715
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:25.715 --> 00:12:28.019
I'd love to know which
of Tupac's top ten rules

00:12:28.019 --> 00:12:30.493
meant the most to you,
had the biggest impact.

00:12:30.493 --> 00:12:32.070
Leave it in the comments
below and I'll join in the

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:32.903
discussion.

00:12:32.903 --> 00:12:34.156
- And tell us which one you want us to

00:12:34.156 --> 00:12:36.505
feature on this channel next time.

00:12:36.505 --> 00:12:38.800
- Thank you guys for
watching. Continue to believe.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.800
And we'll see you soon.

